 "principles": [
  "Walls stay calm and light. Colour comes in small amounts and is used for finding the way.",
  "One accent colour per wing: the seat colour tells a visitor which wing this is.",
  "Seats and tables must stand out from the floor (older eyes need about 3 times the contrast).",
  "No shine: chrome becomes matte metal, glass table tops become wood, black leather becomes tan.",
  "Wood and natural colours (the day-centre study), plants on the walls of the corridors.",
  "Grab rails in a strong colour against the wall. Safety red stays red."
 ],
